1
00:00:00,454 --> 00:00:01,954
Hi everyone, I'm Corentin,

2
00:00:02,020 --> 00:00:04,361
and today it's a quick tutorial
on "coasting".

3
00:00:05,001 --> 00:00:09,068
To "coast", you first need
to know how to "glide".

4
00:00:09,281 --> 00:00:13,039
If you can't do that yet,
there's a short "glide" tutorial

5
00:00:13,105 --> 00:00:16,474
on the Commission Nationale
de Monocycle website.

6
00:00:16,974 --> 00:00:18,420
So what is "coasting"?

7
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:23,560
It's balancing without touching
the pedals or the wheel.

8
00:00:24,694 --> 00:00:27,081
There are two basic kinds of "coasting".

9
00:00:27,226 --> 00:00:30,948
I'll show you a few
to get you hooked on "coasting".

10
00:00:31,014 --> 00:00:32,701
That was "two-foot coasting".

11
00:00:32,761 --> 00:00:36,960
Here's "one-foot coasting, crossed".

12
00:00:41,037 --> 00:00:43,204
This is "stand-up coasting".

13
00:00:44,017 --> 00:00:45,990
This is the "no foot side coast".

14
00:00:47,497 --> 00:00:52,470
Here's "switch-foot coasting",
ending with a little "backward coast".

15
00:00:55,011 --> 00:00:56,650
And the "coasting toe point spin".

16
00:00:59,884 --> 00:01:03,431
Note there are two kinds of "coasting".

17
00:01:03,557 --> 00:01:05,275
There's "two-foot coasting",

18
00:01:05,341 --> 00:01:09,232
which freestylers tend to prefer,
and "one-foot coasting",

19
00:01:09,298 --> 00:01:12,460
which flatland riders tend to prefer,
since their unicycles are lower

20
00:01:12,526 --> 00:01:15,164
and it's hard for them
to get both feet on the frame.

21
00:01:15,771 --> 00:01:18,223
So go with whatever suits you.

22
00:01:19,344 --> 00:01:21,957
The easiest way to start
is to have someone tow you.

23
00:01:22,037 --> 00:01:24,617
I was on my own here,
so nobody was towing me.

24
00:01:25,811 --> 00:01:28,247
If you're practicing alone
with no one to tow you,

25
00:01:28,313 --> 00:01:30,991
the best thing is to hold your arms
in this position,

26
00:01:31,057 --> 00:01:32,916
as if the police were arresting you.

27
00:01:33,039 --> 00:01:35,945
Then, if your butt goes back,
lean your upper body forward.

28
00:01:36,057 --> 00:01:39,398
If your butt goes forward,
lean your upper body back.

29
00:01:39,691 --> 00:01:41,117
It's even more obvious

30
00:01:41,183 --> 00:01:43,371
with your foot,
when you're on "one foot".

31
00:01:43,844 --> 00:01:45,727
I exaggerated the movement here

32
00:01:45,793 --> 00:01:49,218
so you could see it clearly,
but normally it's much smaller.

33
00:01:49,284 --> 00:01:52,864
Now I'll show you the different ways
to get back on the pedals.

34
00:01:52,904 --> 00:01:54,725
You can go back into a "glide".

35
00:01:55,017 --> 00:01:56,023
That's the easiest one.

36
00:01:57,124 --> 00:02:00,130
Putting your feet back
one at a time.

37
00:02:03,144 --> 00:02:06,600
And finally, both feet back at once.

38
00:02:06,624 --> 00:02:09,565
There's no secret:
like every other trick,

39
00:02:09,631 --> 00:02:13,344
you have to practice it over and over,
and eventually you'll get it.

40
00:02:14,151 --> 00:02:15,938
Thanks for watching.

41
00:02:16,351 --> 00:02:20,277
If you have any questions about anything,

42
00:02:20,343 --> 00:02:24,004
or just want to show off your progress,
feel free to send me your videos.

43
00:02:24,230 --> 00:02:25,758
I'll be happy to reply.

44
00:02:26,357 --> 00:02:27,383
Ciao!

